cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code or its findings, please cite the paper.
title: >-
  Code and analysis for "Aggregate Accuracy Conceals an Acquisition-Level
  Failure in a Public Radar Target Recognition Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Session-grouped evaluation of the Real Doppler RAD-DAR database. Twenty of
  twenty-one drone acquisitions reach out-of-fold recall between 0.90 and
  0.99; one reaches 0.249. Held out of training entirely, recall on a
  held-back half is 0.157, rising to 0.967 once the other half is in
  training. The repository contains the full pipeline, the unit tests, a
  synthetic self-test that runs without the archive, and a verification
  script that reruns every experiment and checks each number the paper
  states.
type: software
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23118075
